THREAT INTELLIGENCE ADVISORY — Rdp Ransomware campaign
======================================================

Distribution: TLP:AMBER   Analyst handoff   Confidence: HIGH   (IOCs are defanged)
Affected host: rdp-prod-01   Suspected origin IP: 198.51.100.92

1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY
An external actor executed a multi-stage post-compromise sequence. Endpoint alerting covered only part of it; several persistence and anti-forensic actions were silent. Map every on-disk finding to the ATT&CK techniques below and flag which are NOT in the SAS alert feed.

2. ATT&CK TECHNIQUE MAPPING (MITRE ATT&CK Enterprise)
   T1110      Brute Force                                [credential-access]  step 1: RDP brute force
   T1021.001  Remote Desktop Protocol                    [lateral-movement]  step 2: RDP logon
   T1059.001  PowerShell                                 [execution]  step 3: PowerShell execution
   T1486      Data Encrypted for Impact                  [impact]  step 4: ransomware encryption
   T1053.005  Scheduled Task                             [execution]  step 5: scheduled task persistence
   T1547.001  Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder         [persistence]  step 6: Run key persistence
   T1543.003  Windows Service                            [persistence]  step 7: malicious service
   T1070.001  Clear Windows Event Logs                   [defense-evasion]  step 8: Windows event log clear

