[?2004l[?2004hroot@8784182002ee:/app# cat << 'EOF' > /app/intrusion-report.md
[?2004l[?2004h> # Incident Intrusion Report: Post-Compromise Forensic Analysis
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Executive Summary
[?2004lows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`).
   - SHA-256 (`SOFTWARE`): `b08f4418b698c040964ae535a0ed3ea9c7b2ca83ffb0d[?2004h> On 2026-08-13 at 03:20 UTC, host `rdp-prod-01` running Windows Server 2022 (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`) was compromised by an external threat actor. The initial entry vector was RDP credential brute-forcing (`T1110`) originating from IP `198.51.100.92` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`), facilitated by Network Level Authentication (NLA) being disabled (`UserAuthentication = 0`) (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Following successful RDP authentication (`T1021.001`), the attacker established multiple persistence mechanisms, deployed ransomware (`T1486`), performed C2 beaconing to `update-rdp.example.cn` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`), and cleared the Security event log (EventID 1102) (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx`) to cover their tracks.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> While initial security alerts (`/sas/alerts.json:1`) flagged the ransomware binary, scheduled task, and malicious driver service, forensic analysis of `/disk` revealed additional **silent persistence** (Registry Run key) and **silent defense evasion** (Security log clearing) that bypassed initial automated detections.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Attack Chain Analysis
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Step 1: External Credential Access & Lateral Movement
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Techniques**: MITRE ATT&CK T1110 (Brute Force) & T1021.001 (Remote Desktop Protocol)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence & Findings**: The attacker targeted the exposed RDP interface on host `rdp-prod-01` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`). Because NLA was disabled (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg`), the attacker performed password brute-forcing from origin IP `198.51.100.92` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`) and obtained interactive access.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Step 2: Execution & Payload Dropping
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Techniques**: MITRE ATT&CK T1059.001 (PowerShell Execution) & T1486 (Data Encrypted for Impact)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence & Findings**: Upon gaining access, the attacker dropped and executed a ransomware binary at `/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe` (`/sas/alerts.json:3`, `/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe`). The ransomware sample encrypts user files with a `.locked` extension and drops a ransom note. Strings in the binary revealed embedded Monero mining/ransomware telemetry including pool `stratum+tcp://xmr.rdp.evil:3333` and wallet `4A0000000000000000000e4435cc95c5` (`/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe`).
[?2004l[?2004h>   - SHA-256 (`svc.exe`): `4f8a5c4380a18bca293c7e9130caf957973cc733e9b2c32c2e5240aa9e2c2dae` (`/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe`)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Step 3: Persistence Establishment
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Scheduled Task Persistence (Alerted)**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Technique**: MITRE ATT&CK T1053.005 (Scheduled Task)
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Evidence**: Scheduled task `UpdateHelper` configured via `schtasks` to execute `/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe` every 5 minutes (`/sas/alerts.json:11`, `/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - SHA-256 (`UpdateHelper`): `2c2313138723024ae31eb2d8c399cc3f47ffd7221937f098247629dba83d730d` (`/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper`)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Malicious Service Persistence (Alerted)**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Technique**: MITRE ATT&CK T1543.003 (Windows Service)
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Evidence**: Malicious Windows service `svc-helper` registered to load driver file `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys` at system boot (`/sas/alerts.json:19`, `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys`). Strings confirm helper service capability linked to Monero wallet `4A0000000000000000000e4435cc95c5` (`/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - SHA-256 (`svc-helper.sys`): `8525c122105c20ecbf866f40d8d60ad1fbbe21fd07a6b77c79182631931ede86` (`/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys`)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Registry Run Key Persistence (SILENT / UNALERTED)**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Technique**: MITRE ATT&CK T1547.001 (Registry Run Keys / Startup Folder)
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Evidence**: Examination of the SOFTWARE registry hive (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`) revealed an unalerted Run key value `svc` set to auto-execute `C:\Users\Public\svc.exe` upon user logon. This finding was omitted from the automated alert feed (`/sas/alerts.json:1`) and was uncovered via forensic disk analysis (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - SHA-256 (`SOFTWARE`): `b08f4418b698c040964ae535a0ed3ea9c7b2ca83ffb0d32bd5c536c63e3c4971` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Step 4: Defense Evasion & Anti-Forensics (SILENT / UNALERTED)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Technique**: MITRE ATT&CK T1070.001 (Clear Windows Event Logs)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Evidence**: The attacker cleared the Security event log (`EventID 1102`) to erase records of interactive logons and process creations (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx`). This anti-forensic action was silent in the primary alert feed (`/sas/alerts.json:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Recovery**: Residual forensic evidence recovered from backup security registry hive `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak` and system log `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx` confirmed C2 beaconing activity to `198.51.100.92` (`update-rdp.example.cn`) and Administrator credential cache access (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Observed Entities & Indicators of Compromise (IoCs)
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> | Indicator Type | Value | Evidence Citation |
[?2004l[?2004h> |---|---|---|
[?2004l[?2004h> | Source IP / C2 IP | `198.51.100.92` | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`, `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | C2 Domain | `update-rdp.example.cn` | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:6`, `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Mining Pool | `stratum+tcp://xmr.rdp.evil:3333` | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:7`, `/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Monero Wallet | `4A0000000000000000000e4435cc95c5` | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:8`, `/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Ransomware Binary | `/Users/Public/svc.exe` | `/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe`, `/sas/alerts.json:3` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Scheduled Task | `UpdateHelper` | `/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper`, `/sas/alerts.json:11` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Driver Service | `svc-helper` (`/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys`) | `/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys`, `/sas/alerts.json:19` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Registry Run Key | `HKLM\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Run\svc` | `/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE` |
[?2004l[?2004h> | Cleared Log Event | Security EventID 1102 | `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx` |
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
[?2004l[?2004hroot@8784182002ee:/app# cat << 'EOF' > /app/vuln-report.md
[?2004l[?2004h> # Vulnerability Assessment Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Executive Summary
[?2004l[?2004h> Analysis of host `rdp-prod-01` and security telemetry confirms that **no software vulnerabilities (CVEs) were exploited** to gain initial access or execute remote code during this incident. The vulnerability scan feed (`/sas/vulns.json:1`) returned an empty array (`[]`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> The initial access vector was brute-force credential exploitation against exposed RDP (`T1110` / `T1021.001`), enabled by a configuration flaw (disabled Network Level Authentication) rather than an unpatched software flaw.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Vulnerability Telemetry Evaluation
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Vulnerability Feed**: `/sas/vulns.json:1` contains `[]` (empty list).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Software Inventory**: Analysis of `/disk/ProgramData/Package Cache/inventory.csv` and system configuration (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`) showed standard operating system components on Windows Server 2022 with no unpatched exploitable software vulnerabilities identified.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Rejection of Claimed CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep)
[?2004l[?2004h> Initial handoff materials and draft change ticket (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:10`) suggested patching `CVE-2019-0708` (BlueKeep).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> Forensic analysis conclusively refutes this claim based on the following evidence:
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Operating System Incompatibility**: The target host is running Windows Server 2022 (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`). CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep) is a Remote Code Execution vulnerability in Remote Desktop Services that affects older operating systems (Windows 7, Windows Server 2008, Windows Server 2008 R2). Windows Server 2022 is structurally immune to CVE-2019-0708.
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Absence in Vulnerability Telemetry**: `/sas/vulns.json:1` reports zero vulnerabilities.
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Observed Entry Mechanism**: Forensic artifacts in CTI intelligence (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13`) and registry baseline (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg`) confirm that the entry vector was RDP credential brute-forcing (`T1110`) resulting from Network Level Authentication (NLA) being disabled (`UserAuthentication = 0`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Conclusion & Confidence Level
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Vulnerability-Driven Access**: Explicitly Absent.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Confidence**: HIGH (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:3`, `/sas/vulns.json:1`, `/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Remediation Focus**: Shift resources away from non-applicable software patching (e.g. BlueKeep) toward credential hygiene, RDP exposure restriction, and enforcing Network Level Authentication.
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
[?2004l[?2004hroot@8784182002ee:/app# cat << 'EOF' > /app/baseline-report.md
[?2004l[?2004h> # Baseline & Security Configuration Analysis Report
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Executive Summary
[?2004l[?2004h> A post-compromise baseline evaluation of host `rdp-prod-01` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`) revealed critical configuration weaknesses and logging blind spots that facilitated initial access and allowed attacker persistence and anti-forensics to go undetected.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Weaknesses Identified
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 1. Disabled Network Level Authentication (NLA) on RDP
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Check ID**: `CHK-06` / `BAS-01` (`/sas/baseline.json:3`, `/sas/alerts.json:27`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding**: Inspection of the terminal services registry dump `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg` shows:
[?2004l[?2004h>   `"Value0"="RDP UserAuthentication = 0 (NLA disabled), connections allowed"` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4`)
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact**: Disabling NLA permits unauthenticated RDP session negotiation prior to credential validation, exposing the RDP service directly to external automated brute-force attacks (`T1110`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt:13`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 2. Direct Public Internet RDP Exposure
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding**: The host was directly accessible from public IP `198.51.100.92` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`) without network-level filtering, VPN requirements, or multi-factor authentication (MFA).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact**: Enabled unrestricted remote brute-force attempts until valid credentials were guessed.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 3. Lack of Registry Run Key Persistence Monitoring
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding**: The system permitted modifications to auto-start registry locations (`HKLM\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Run`) without generating security alerts (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`, `/sas/alerts.json:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact**: The attacker established silent persistence via entry `svc` pointing to `/Users/Public/svc.exe` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`) which remained active and unflagged by endpoint monitoring.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### 4. Unmonitored Event Log Manipulation
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Finding**: The Security log was cleared (Event ID 1102) (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx`). No real-time security alert was generated for log clearance.
[?2004l[?2004h> - **Impact**: Allowed the attacker to execute anti-forensic log wiping without immediate SOC intervention.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Baseline Compliance Recommendations
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. Enforce Network Level Authentication (`UserAuthentication = 1`) on all RDP listeners (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. Implement host-based and network perimeter firewalls to restrict RDP access to authorized internal networks / VPN gateways.
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. Configure Sysmon or EDR registry modification rules to alert on changes to `CurrentVersion\Run` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 4. Configure Windows Event Log forwarding and SIEM alerts for Event ID 1102 (Log Cleared) (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx`).
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
[?2004l[?2004hroot@8784182002ee:/app# cat << 'EOF' > /app/remediation-plan.md
[?2004l[?2004h> # Incident Remediation & Recovery Plan
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Executive Summary
[?2004l[?2004h> This remediation plan outlines prioritised, verifiable actions to isolate, quarantine, remove persistent artifacts, and harden host `rdp-prod-01` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`) following an RDP brute-force and ransomware compromise. In accordance with DFIR standards, containment actions prefer quarantine and backup over immediate deletion.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> This document reconciles and corrects draft change ticket `CHG-9792` (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md:1`).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Reconciled Change Ticket CHG-9792
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> | # | Action | Target | Status | Note & Evidence Citation |
[?2004l[?2004h> |---|--------|--------|--------|--------------------------|
[?2004l` (`/d[?2004h> | 1 | Block source IP inbound | `198.51.100.92` | proposed | **CORRECTED IP**: Replaced stale IP `203.0.113.9` with verified attacker C2 / origin IP `198.51.100.92` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`, `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`). |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 2 | Enforce RDP NLA & Restrict Access | RDP (`RDP-Tcp`) | proposed | **REJECTED CVE-2019-0708**: Host is Windows Server 2022 (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`), immune to BlueKeep. Replaced with RDP NLA enforcement (`UserAuthentication = 1`) and firewall restrictions (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4`, `/sas/baseline.json:3`). |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 3 | Reject Linux cron job removal | `/var/spool/cron/root` | REJECTED | **DOWNGRADED FROM DONE**: Prior shift marked DONE without evidence. Target host is Windows Server 2022 (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`), not Linux. No cron spool exists (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`). |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 4 | Quarantine Ransomware Binary | `/Users/Public/svc.exe` | proposed | **ADDED**: Backup/quarantine binary `/Users/Public/svc.exe` before terminating process (`/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe`, `/sas/alerts.json:3`). |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 5 | Remove Scheduled Task Persistence | `/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper` | proposed | **ADDED**: Unregister scheduled task `UpdateHelper` executing `svc.exe` every 5 min (`/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper`, `/sas/alerts.json:11`). |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 6 | Disable & Quarantine Driver Service | `/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys` | proposed | **ADDED**: Stop and disable service `svc-helper`, quarantine driver binary `/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys` (`/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys`, `/sas/alerts.json:19`). |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 7 | Remove Silent Registry Run Key | `HKLM\SOFTWARE\...\Run\svc` | proposed | **ADDED (SILENT PERSISTENCE)**: Remove registry Run key `svc` pointing to `C:\Users\Public\svc.exe` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`). |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 8 | Password Reset & Hash Invalidation | Administrator Account | proposed | **ADDED**: Force password reset for Administrator and invalidate compromised cached credentials (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`). |
[?2004l[?2004h> | 9 | Enable SIEM Alerts for Log Clearing | `Security.evtx` (Event 1102) | proposed | **ADDED (SILENT ANTI-FORENSICS)**: Deploy alert rule for Security event log clearance (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx`). |
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ---
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ## Prioritised Phase Breakdown & Verification
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 1: Isolation & Containment (Immediate)
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Network Firewall Block**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Action**: Add inbound drop rule for `198.51.100.92` on perimeter firewall and host Windows Firewall (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt:5`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Verification**: Run `Test-NetConnection -ComputerName 198.51.100.92` to confirm zero outbound/inbound connectivity.
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **RDP Exposure Mitigation**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Action**: Modify registry key `HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Terminal Server\WinStations\RDP-Tcp` setting `UserAuthentication = 1` (enable NLA) (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RDP-Tcp.reg:4`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Verification**: Query registry via `reg query "HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Terminal Server\WinStations\RDP-Tcp" /v UserAuthentication` and verify output is `0x1`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 2: Persistence Quarantine & Remediation (High Priority)
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Process & Binary Quarantine**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Action**: Terminate process `svc.exe`. Move `/Users/Public/svc.exe` to isolated quarantine directory `C:\Quarantine\` with access control restrictions (`/disk/Users/Public/svc.exe`). Do not delete directly.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Verification**: Confirm process is absent in Task Manager / `Get-Process svc` and file moved to `C:\Quarantine\`.
[?2004l[?2004h> 2. **Scheduled Task Removal**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Action**: Delete scheduled task `UpdateHelper` via `schtasks /Delete /TN "UpdateHelper" /F` (`/disk/Windows/System32/Tasks/UpdateHelper`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Verification**: Run `schtasks /Query /TN "UpdateHelper"` and confirm task not found.
[?2004l[?2004h> 3. **Malicious Driver Service Remediation**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Action**: Stop service `svc-helper` (`sc stop svc-helper`), set startup type to disabled (`sc config svc-helper start= disabled`), and move `/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys` to `C:\Quarantine\` (`/disk/Windows/System32/svc-helper.sys`). Delete service definition via `sc delete svc-helper`.
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Verification**: Run `sc query svc-helper` to confirm service does not exist.
[?2004l[?2004h> 4. **Silent Registry Run Key Removal**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Action**: Remove value `svc` from `HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Run` via `reg delete "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Run" /v svc /f` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/SOFTWARE`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Verification**: Run `reg query "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Run" /v svc` and verify key not found.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 3: Identity & Access Recovery (Medium Priority)
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Credential Invalidation**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Action**: Change Administrator password to strong complex passphrase (>20 chars). Invalidate active Kerberos tickets (`klist purge`) and clear LSA cached secrets (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Verification**: Confirm new password required for all interactive and network logons.
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> ### Phase 4: Monitoring & Anti-Forensics Hardening (Long Term)
[?2004l[?2004h> 1. **Security Log Clearance Auditing**:
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Action**: Enable Windows Event Forwarding (WEF) and configure SIEM alert for Event ID 1102 in Security.evtx (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/Security.evtx`).
[?2004l[?2004h>    - **Verification**: Trigger benign log clear event in lab environment and verify SIEM alert fires within 60 seconds.
[?2004l[?2004h> EOF
